t', methods=['POST'])\ndef add_to_cart():\n    data = request.get_json()\n    item_title = data.get('title')\n    username = session.get('username')\n    if username and item_title:\n        write_cart(username, item_title)  # Add the item to the user's cart\n        return '', 200  # Return a success response\n    return '', 400  # Return a bad request response if something goes wrong\n\n\n### Instructions for Implementation:\n1. Open the app.py file.\n2. Add the above add_to_cart() function to handle the POST request for adding items to the cart.\n3. Ensure that the function is placed before the if __name__ == '__main__': block.\n4. Test the functionality by running the application and trying to add an item to the cart from the item details page.\n\nBy implementing this change, you will ensure that the application functions correctly when users attempt to add items to their shopping cart."} |
